<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109808" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφάπτω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπάπτω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set on fire from underneath,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπῆψαν τὴν ἀκρόπολιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.176
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφῆψε δῶμ᾽ ἀνηφαίστῳ πυρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					621
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1618
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. πυράν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.52
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις ὑφάπτεται πυρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1274
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃς</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμάξας</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἔδει ἐν καιρῷ ὑφαφθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aen.Tact.
					28.7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὕρωμεν</span> (i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ομεν</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> τὰς θύρας . . ὑφημ&lt;μ&gt;ένας
					φωτί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					1201.10
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., <i>inflame unperceived,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς θεωμένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					5.1.16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>light underneath,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ, φλόγα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Phal.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristaenet.
				2.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ νικέων ὑφαπτέτω τὰ
			ἱερά</span> the winner (in the race) <i>shall light</i> the
			sacred lamps, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				71.16
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>): abs., <i>light a fire
				under</i> or <i>in</i> a place, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				730
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>B.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>tie</i> or <i>bind under,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ δειρὴν ἁψαμένη</span>
			<i>tying a rope round</i> her neck, hanging herself, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aet.
				3.33
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
